{%- comment %} The Sitemap directive is independent of any User-agent group
   (sitemaps.org/protocol.html), so it sits on its own.

   /opengraph/ is NOT disallowed on purpose. Those pages carry meta robots
   noindex, and a crawler forbidden from fetching a page can never read the
   noindex inside it — disallowing them would preserve exactly the indexing this
   theme is trying to prevent. Blocking crawling and asking for de-indexing are
   opposite instructions; only one of them works here.
{% endcomment -%}
User-agent: *
Allow: /

Sitemap: {{ site.url }}/sitemap.xml
